  "groom_note": "Fill (20261011): the 20261010 locks were flat ribbons at random depths in the envelope, clumped to points from mid-length, so in game (0.022 cm strands, hard sun, deep shadows) they read as flat bright clumps over near-black crevices and the crown edge broke into see-through tips. Every guide and lock of 20261010 is kept (seed, guides and children unchanged). extra_children adds 60 strands per guide from an independent seed (77,550 to 110,550 strands); each child blends its 6 nearest guides with Gaussian weights (blend_sigma 1 cm) instead of near-copying the nearest; clump 0.75 gathers late (clump_power 3: broad to near the tip); lock_thickness 3.5 mm gives a lock depth through its layer. strand_radius scales the review render to the new count (the game sets its own width). Measured in the game-look proxy (render_painted_head.py --light sun --hair-shader diffuse at the game's strand width): see docs/ENNIX_REBUILD.md, Groom fill.",
